ype">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Beornwulf was king of Mercia from 823 to 826, after displacing Ceolwulf I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/beowulf"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/beowulf.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Beowulf</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Beowulf is an Old English epic poem of about 3,180 lines, preserved in a single manuscript copied around 1000; its date of composition is debated.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/beqaa-valley"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/beqaa-valley.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Beqaa Valley</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Beqaa Valley is a fertile high plain in eastern Lebanon between the Mount Lebanon and Anti-Lebanon ranges, drained by the Litani and Orontes rivers.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/bera-count-of-barcelona"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bera-count-of-barcelona.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Bera, Count of Barcelona</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Bera was the first count of Barcelona after the Franks captured the city in 801, a Goth probably descended from William of Gellone.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/berar"><span class="enc-name">Berar</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Berar is a historical region of central India, now the western part of the Vidarbha division of Maharashtra, around Amravati and Akola.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berat"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berat</span><span 